@SonicPulse.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5045

### POST — valid detection -> 201, Location header, { "id": ... }
POST {{SonicPulse.Api_HostAddress}}/api/detections
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "peakDbfs": -8.5,
  "latitude": 45.8010,
  "longitude": 15.9700,
  "gpsAccuracy": 12.0,
  "peakTimeClient": "2026-07-02T14:31:07Z"
}

### POST — invalid payload -> 400 (latitude out of range, positive dBFS)
POST {{SonicPulse.Api_HostAddress}}/api/detections
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "peakDbfs": 5,
  "latitude": 200,
  "longitude": 15.9700,
  "gpsAccuracy": 12.0,
  "peakTimeClient": "2026-07-02T14:31:07Z"
}

### GET by id (paste id from first response) -> 200
GET {{SonicPulse.Api_HostAddress}}/api/detections/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### GET nonexistent id -> 404
GET {{SonicPulse.Api_HostAddress}}/api/detections/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999

### GET by device -> 200, { items, nextCursor }, newest first
GET {{SonicPulse.Api_HostAddress}}/api/devices/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111/detections

### GET next page (paste nextCursor from previous response)
GET {{SonicPulse.Api_HostAddress}}/api/devices/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111/detections?limit=2&cursor=12345

### GET nonexistent device -> 200, empty items list (not 404 — a device isn't a resource we look up)
GET {{SonicPulse.Api_HostAddress}}/api/devices/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999/detections
